    "view": {
      "value": "<div class=\"contentLayout2\">\n<div class=\"columnLayout two-right-sidebar\" data-layout=\"two-right-sidebar\">\n<div class=\"cell normal\" data-type=\"normal\">\n<div class=\"innerCell\">\n<h2 id=\"Registration-AbouttheFeature\">About the Feature</h2><div>Patient Registration provides the ability to start a patient file at a hospital. Most hospitals have a front desk where patients have to register before starting medical interactions such as consultation, lab tests, admission, procedures etc. The Registration Module in Bahmni will be used at the front desk to capture patient information that can be collected by non-clinical staff. </div><h2 id=\"Registration-UsedBy\"><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">Used By</span></h2><p><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">The person at the Registration desk of the facility would predominantly use </span><span>this module.</span></p><h2 id=\"Registration-HowisitUsed?\"><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">How is it Used?</span></h2><div><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\"> </span>The Registration Module allows for searching existing patients, adding new patients to the system, capturing name, photograph, address and specific attributes that the hospital may be interested in. It can also be configured to capture clinical information such as height, weight etc depending on a hospital workflow. </div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"cell aside\" data-type=\"aside\">\n<div class=\"innerCell\">\n<div class=\"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-tip conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"true\" data-macro-id=\"6462b5e2-1d86-451d-a8c5-c39c2f99335c\" data-macro-name=\"tip\"><span class=\"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-approve confluence-information-macro-icon\"> </span><div class=\"confluence-information-macro-body\"><p><strong><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">Bahmni configuration for each implementation can vary drastically. As the screens and workflows are not constant across all installations of Bahmni, we have refrained from prescribing them. </span></strong></p><p><strong><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\">Please refer to the Guides below for further details about the feature.</span></strong></p></div></div><div class=\"panel conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"true\" data-macro-id=\"0add60ca-db50-405a-bfd6-90945fbc2b0b\" data-macro-name=\"panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;background-color: #668D3C;color: white;\"><b>Feature Details</b></div><div class=\"panelContent\">\n<p><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\"><a href=\"/wiki/spaces/BAH/pages/32604190/Patient+Registration\" data-linked-resource-id=\"32604190\" data-linked-resource-version=\"38\" data-linked-resource-type=\"page\">Registration - Feature Guide</a></span></p>\n</div></div><div class=\"panel conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"true\" data-macro-id=\"3fe3feef-06ea-4aac-b9a1-a6bbe83b0bec\" data-macro-name=\"panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;background-color: #668D3C;color: white;\"><b>Implemnentation Details</b></div><div class=\"panelContent\">\n<p><span class=\"legacy-color-text-default\"><a href=\"/wiki/spaces/BAH/pages/32014487/Patient+Registration+Module\" data-linked-resource-id=\"32014487\" data-linked-resource-version=\"25\" data-linked-resource-type=\"page\">Registration - Implementer's Guide</a></span></p>\n</div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
